Let $D$ be a filter on $\omega$ containing the Fréchet filter (the filter of cofinite sets). For $f,g\in\omega^\omega$ write $f<_D g$ to mean $\{n\in\omega:f(n)<g(n)\}\in D$, and similarly $\leq_D$ and $=_D$. A subset $A\subseteq\omega$ is $D$-positive if $\omega\setminus A\notin D$; for such $A$, let $D+A$ denote the filter generated by $D\cup\{A\}$.

Let $\delta,\theta$ be regular infinite cardinals. A weakly peculiar $(\delta,\theta)$-$D$-cut in $\omega^\omega$ is a pair of sequences $\langle f_\alpha:\alpha<\delta\rangle$ and $\langle g_\beta:\beta<\theta\rangle$ in $\omega^\omega$ such that:
(i) $\alpha<\alpha'<\delta\Rightarrow f_\alpha<_D f_{\alpha'}$;
(ii) $\beta<\beta'<\theta\Rightarrow g_{\beta'}<_D g_\beta$;
(iii) $f_\alpha<_D g_\beta$ for all $\alpha<\delta$, $\beta<\theta$;
(iv) there is no $f\in\omega^\omega$ and no $D$-positive set $A$ such that $f_\alpha<_{D+A} f<_{D+A} g_\beta$ for all $\alpha<\delta$, $\beta<\theta$.

Define
$$\mathrm{spec}_{uq}=\{\kappa\text{ regular}: \text{for every filter }D\text{ extending the Fréchet filter, if there exist weakly peculiar }(\kappa,\theta_0)\text{- and }(\kappa,\theta_1)\text{-}D\text{-cuts, then }\theta_0=\theta_1\}.$$

Define $\mathrm{spec}_{uqm}$ analogously, but require the equality $\theta_0=\theta_1$ to be witnessed by an internal order-preserving partial map between the corresponding decreasing sequences: that is, there exists a partial function $h$, definable in a uniform internal sense from the data, which is order-preserving and provides a cofinal correspondence between $\langle g^0_\beta:\beta<\theta_0\rangle$ and $\langle g^1_\beta:\beta<\theta_1\rangle$ modulo $D$.

Question: Is $\mathrm{spec}_{uq}=\mathrm{spec}_{uqm}$? If not, are the cardinal invariants $\min(\mathrm{spec}_{uq})$ and $\min(\mathrm{spec}_{uqm})$ (and analogous derived invariants) nonetheless equal?

